    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254-a4">

                <pb facs="0371" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg265"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure C.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Capt. Schley to the
                            intendente of Valparaiso</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. Baltimore</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">First
                                Rate</hi>),<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Valparaiso</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1891-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December 9, 1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to request that you will
                    inform me whether his honor the judge of the criminal court will require any
                    further testimony from the men of the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> in
                    the process now pending relative to the disorders of the 16th of October.</p>
                <p>I would be greatly obliged if your excellency will favor me with this information
                    at the earliest practicable moment.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Schley</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain Commanding</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
